# The files release/package.sh fetches, one line per file, "<sha256>  <url>". Where the pins came from:
# rhino and asm sources jars, Maven Central's published .sha256 (and .sha1) for each; the jzlib sources
# jar, Central's .sha1 (it publishes no .sha256), which it matches, and it is byte for byte the copy in
# the Gradle cache. The OpenJDK LICENSE at the pinned jdk25u revision: two downloads a day apart agree
# (release 2026.09.27-1's copy and a fresh one). The cldr-json LICENSE at tag 37.0.0: from the download;
# GitHub publishes no checksum, and a tag can move, which this pin would catch.
RELEASE_INPUTS_SHA256="
4b9abebc4338048a7c2dc184e9f800deb349366bdf28eb23c2677a77b4c87726  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openjdk/jdk25u/6c48f4ed707bf0b15f9b6098de30db8aae6fa40f/LICENSE
d3be964dc5fd505b79432a3d57659420d3ad6a8be9eea8406e1b0a4e7c6f06f2  https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/mozilla/rhino/1.7.15/rhino-1.7.15-sources.jar
c6294794f956f21e2b252a9bf65a96ce0489fb4c0f978447d85c8a75e485b633  https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/ow2/asm/asm/9.8/asm-9.8-sources.jar
